<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Safi of Persia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1629">1629</a>–<a href="/years/1642">1642</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Shah Safi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Safi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, known as Shah Safi, was the Safavid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1629 to 1642 and the grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a>. His reign saw purges of officials and members of the royal family and the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> place his reign at the start of the empire's gradual decline after the achievements of Abbas I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/safi-of-persia.jpg" alt="Safi of Persia" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shah_Safi_I_of_Persia_(reigned_1629-1642)_on_horseback_carrying_a_mace(_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
